{"availability":"available","full":"prnthh/react-three-game","name":"react-three-game","description":"Batteries included game engine for react-three-fiber.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":28,"forks":3,"created":"2025-12-03T20:13:07Z","updated":"2026-10-04T08:15:29Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"http://prnth.com/react-three-game/","topics":["game-engine","rapier","rapier3d","react-three-fiber","react-three-fiber-game","three-js"],"demo":"https://prnth.com/react-three-game/demo/customcomponent","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:15:40.231Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:15:40.231Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:15:40.231Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:15:40.231Z","stars":28,"forks":3}],"technologies":["React","Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A game creation toolbox for the web. Build games with JavaScript and Three.js, WebGPU rendering, and a visual scene editor.","We use React and React Three Fiber to make behavior reusable and easy to compose. Start with small components, then build on them as your game grows. Assemble scenes in the editor and save them as JSON prefabs. Agents can help compose and tune scenes through the editor API too.","A scene is a JSON document containing nodes (scene objects) and component settings. Calling registerComponent makes a behavior and its editable settings available. The window API lets agents inspect and edit this document. Reusable scene documents are called prefabs; they store settings. Behavior code usually stays in the application; the built-in Runtime component can also store JavaScript directly in a prefab."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/prnthh/react-three-game/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"6a6ff054a3b8f0132be105ce8af4120f3df788fa4ab12a78c339434d23a6ecb0","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T08:15:40.362Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:15:40.362Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"tex